# Copy to .env.local. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Local values come from `supabase start`, which prints them once it is up.
# Hosted values are in the project dashboard under Project Settings → API.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public. These reach the browser, which is correct: the publishable key does
# nothing on its own. Every permission it has is decided by row level security
# against the signed-in member's session.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321

# New projects issue sb_publishable_…; older ones an `anon` JWT. Either works —
# set whichever one your project gave you.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server only. This key bypasses row level security completely.
#
# It is used for exactly two things: signing short-lived URLs for private
# storage objects after the database has already authorised the caller, and
# scheduled maintenance with no user attached. If a page needs it to render,
# something is wrong with a policy.
#
# Must never be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local verification harness (npm run db:verify / db:types). Names a throwaway
# database on your own PostgreSQL server; nothing else reads it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DB=samaj_setu_verify

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not used yet, and deliberately so:
#
#   * No SMS provider. This release sends no OTP — identity is established by
#     admin review of the birth certificate (spec §3). Adding Twilio or MSG91
#     credentials here is step one of turning OTP on; see the comment above
#     [auth.sms] in supabase/config.toml for the rest.
#   * No push or email provider. public.notification_outbox queues messages and
#     nothing drains it. Rows there mean "queued", never "delivered".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
